{"id":"jj-game","name":"jj-game","aliases":[],"caption":"A LaTeX class to construct Jeopardy-like games","authors":[{"id":"story","active":true}],"copyright":[{"owner":"D. P. Story","year":"2000-2016"}],"license":"lppl1","version":{"number":"3.1","date":"2016-11-24"},"descriptions":[{"language":null,"text":"<p>\n      The class defines a Jeopardy-like game; question answers may be\n      multiple choice, or text or mathematics <q>fill-ins<\u002fq>.\n    <\u002fp>\n  <p>\n      The basic game can be constructed using dvipsone,\n      <ref refid=\"dvips\">dvips<\u002fref>,\n      <ref refid=\"pdftex\">pdftex<\u002fref> or\n      <ref refid=\"dvipdfm\">dvipdfm<\u002fref>. The <q>pro<\u002fq>\n      option of the game works with dvipsone or dvips only, and\n      requires Adobe Acrobat Pro 7.0 (or later), with its distiller.\n    <\u002fp>\n  <p>\n      The game requires the\n      <ref refid=\"acrotex\">AcroTeX education bundle<\u002fref>, and (for\n      the pro option) <ref refid=\"aeb-pro\">AeB pro<\u002fref>.\n    <\u002fp>\n  <p>\n      Also, the <ref refid=\"eforms\">eforms<\u002fref>\n      package dated 2016-08-29 or later is required.\n    <\u002fp>\n  <p>\n      Samples of sources for games are provided.\n    <\u002fp>"}],"documentation":[{"language":null,"details":"Readme","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/jj_game/README.md"},{"language":null,"details":"Package documentation","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/jj_game/doc/jjg_man.pdf"}],"home":"http://www.math.uakron.edu/~dpstory/jj_game.html","ctan":{"path":"/macros/latex/contrib/jj_game","file":true},"miktex":"jj-game","topics":["adobe-distiller","games","class","pdf-forms"]}